meta {
  name: Disconnect
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{baseURL}}/google-calendar/disconnect/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  Revokes the token with Google and clears the signed-in user's own
  google_access_token / google_refresh_token / google_access_token_expires_at
  on GoogleCalendarConnection. google_email (the "connected as ___" address)
  is deliberately left as a record of the last-connected account — check
  google_refresh_token, not google_email, to know if actually connected.
  Always acts on request.user's connection - never a client-supplied id.

  If the signed-in user is the fixed shared calendar organizer
  (google_email == settings.GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID), disconnecting kills
  appointment sync for every center — platform Admin may disconnect; an
  associate must also hold is_admin=True on at least one center assignment.
  Otherwise: 403.

  Method: DELETE
  Path: /google-calendar/disconnect/
  Source: integrations.google_calendar.views.GoogleCalendarDisconnectView
  Auth: Admin or Associate (JWT).
}
